.TH Q 1 "October 21, 2026" "q 0.4.0" "General Commands Manual"

.SH NAME
q \- one-shot Gemini queries and shell commands from the terminal

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B q
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ QUERY ]...

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B q
sends a question to a model and prints the answer.
It asks Google Gemini through the cookies of the account, so no API key is
needed, and it can also talk to the other providers with a token of the user.
.PP
The answer is shown in a frame and copied to the clipboard.
In command mode the model writes a shell command instead, and only that
command is printed and copied.
.PP
The first run opens a browser window for the sign-in of Google and keeps the
cookies of the account, so the later runs start right away.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-command\-mode
Command mode.
Ask the model for a shell command and print only the command.
.TP
.B \-\-reauth
Remove the saved cookies and sign in to Gemini again.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list\-models
List the models the provider offers.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-usage\-limits
Show the usage limits of the account.
Only the provider of the cookies reports them.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-import\-cookies
Import the cookies of the account by hand.
Recommended on Windows, where the automatic import does not work.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-model " \fIMODEL\fR"
The model to use.
Defaults to
.IR gemini-auto ,
which lets the service pick the model.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-stream
Wait for the whole answer instead of printing it as it comes.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug
Print the debug output for troubleshooting.
.TP
.B \-\-rebuild\-venv
Build the Python environment of the tool again.
.TP
.BR \-\-auth\-timeout " \fISECONDS\fR"
How long to wait for the sign-in in the browser window.
Defaults to
.IR 300 .
The maximum is
.IR 86400 .
.TP
.BR \-\-uc " \fIARGS\fR"
Run the answer through the
.B uc
program with the given arguments.
The program always runs with the
.B \-c
flag, which clears the text, and never with
.BR \-s .
A
.B \-c
or
.B \-s
flag in the arguments is ignored.
.TP
.BR \-\-uc\-path " \fIPATH\fR"
The path of the
.B uc
program to run.
Without it the program is looked up in
.B PATH
under the name
.BR uc .
The program at that path runs with the rights of the user, so point it only at
a build you trust.
.TP
.BR \-\-provider " \fIPROVIDER\fR"
The provider of the models to use.
Defaults to
.BR google\-cookies ,
which works through the cookies of the account.
Every other provider needs a token, which the user adds with
.BR \-\-api\-management .
The name may be written in any way, so
.BR openrouter ,
.B open_router
and
.B OpenRouter
mean the same one.
.TP
.B \-\-api\-management
Open the screen that manages the API keys.
The screen shows every token with its middle hidden, and the tokens are typed
in the terminal, so they never reach the history of the shell.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help information.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B q "what changed in the last commit"
Ask the question and print the answer.
.TP
.B q \-c "find the biggest file here"
Ask for a shell command and print only the command.
.TP
.B q \-\-provider openai \-\-model gpt-4o "your question"
Ask a provider that works with a token of the user.
.TP
.B q \-\-api\-management
Add or remove a token.
.TP
.B q \-\-uc "-c -e cp1251" "your question"
Clean the answer of the typographic garbage and keep the Cyrillic text.
.TP
.B q \-l
List the models of the provider.

.SH PROVIDERS
The provider of the cookies of the account is
.BR google\-cookies .
The other providers come from the library that talks to them, so the list
always matches what the tool can do: OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, Groq, Mistral,
DeepSeek, xAI and more, next to the local ones.
.PP
A local server speaks the protocol of the platform it stands for, so it is set
up as that platform with the address of the server.
The address holds no path: the tool adds the path of the platform.
.PP
.EX
http://127.0.0.1:1234
.EE

.SH CONFIGURATION
The optional file
.B q.conf
in the configuration directory holds the defaults.
The options of the command line win over the file.
The options of the file are case-insensitive and may be written with
.BR = ,
with a space, or with
.BR \-\- .
.PP
.EX
model="gemini-auto"
no-stream=true
auth-timeout=600
provider="open_router"
uc="-c -e cp1251"
uc-path="/opt/homebrew/bin/uc"
.EE
.TP
.B model
The model to use.
.TP
.B no\-stream
Wait for the whole answer by default.
.TP
.B auth\-timeout
How long to wait for the sign-in, in seconds.
.TP
.B provider
The provider of the models to use.
.TP
.B uc
The arguments for the
.B uc
program.
.TP
.B uc\-path
The path of the
.B uc
program.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I q.conf
The optional defaults of the tool.
.TP
.I cookies.json
The cookies of the account, with the rights of the user only.
.TP
.I keys.json
The tokens of the providers, with the rights of the user only.
.TP
.I metadata.json
What the tool knows about the account and the versions it has seen.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B Q_CONFIG_DIR
Uses the given directory for the cookies, the metadata, the defaults and the
Python environment of the tool.
.TP
.B Q_DISABLE_CLIPBOARD
Turns off the copy to the clipboard, so a run leaves the clipboard of the user
alone.

